# Python
backend/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Credentials. docker-compose interpolates from a repo-root .env, and README
# and docs/spec.md both tell you to put real endpoint credentials there — so it
# must never be committable. `.env.example` stays tracked as the reference.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backend/.env

# Node / frontend
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/.pnpm-store/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.log

# CA bundles for internal endpoints — environment-specific, see
# backend/certs/README.md
backend/certs/*
!backend/certs/README.md
